            <div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-field-body field--type-text-long field--label-hidden field__item"><p>The Belltown Dome&nbsp;in Grandeur Park&nbsp;has reached the end of&nbsp;its&nbsp;operational life,&nbsp;and the&nbsp;City&nbsp;is inviting residents to help&nbsp;reimagine what&nbsp;the new&nbsp;space could look like.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Public consultations are&nbsp;now underway to understand what matters most to the&nbsp;neighbourhood. The goal is to ensure the site continues to provide accessible, walkable amenities that reflect local needs.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Residents are encouraged to comment on proposed concepts, suggest&nbsp;adjustments&nbsp;or bring forward their own ideas for the space on&nbsp;<a href="https://engage.ottawa.ca/belltown-dome" target="_blank">Engage Ottawa</a>&nbsp;until&nbsp;February&nbsp;26, 2026.</p></div>
      
